  "title": "Extension-routing outliers: an extension routed to a grammar that cannot represent the format",
  "issueId": 913,
  "purpose": "language-detection routes BY EXTENSION, which is right for a dialect and wrong for a format that merely lives beside the language. The parse-success artifact measures the result per lane and cannot separate 'weak grammar on its own language' from 'not that language at all'. This census compares each measured extension bucket against the lane's own pooled canonical rate and convicts only extensions DECLARED `other-format` — the ruling is data in EXTENSION_RELATION, the arithmetic is in the artifact.",
  "method": "Reads validation/m14/results/M14.0.F10.json (per-lane, per-extension file and ERROR-node counts over digest-pinned hash-ordered corpus samples) and the live router (detectLanguageFromPath). canonical = the lane's POOLED `same-language` + `ambiguous-sniff` rate, chosen over largest-bucket so that a lane whose biggest bucket IS its defect cannot launder it. finding = declared other-format AND >= MIN_FILES files AND >= GAP_PTS absolute points AND >= RATIO-fold above canonical.",
